hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"940","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Hisham bin Ammar told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Zuhair bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir. On the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are three whose prayers God does not accept and for whom no good deed is credited: “The absent slave until he returns to his masters and puts his hand in their hands, and the woman whose husband is displeased with her until he is satisfied, and the drunkard until he sobers up.”"
"941","Yahya bin Hakim told us, Abu Dawud told us, Shu’bah told us, Mansour bin Abdul Rahman Al-Ghadani told me, he said: I heard Al-Shu’bi He narrates, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “If a servant remains, his prayer will not be accepted until he returns to his master.”"
